{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' output_contract.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n\nRecord the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n- The selected room for each session.\n- The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n- The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n- Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n\n## `answer/update_response.md`\n\nAfter the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The update source and date.\n- The specific room assignment affected by the update.\n- Which original assignments remain valid and should be preserved.\n- The replacement assignment and why it satisfies the same session requirements.\n- The revised cost effect.\n\n## `answer/final_room_plan.md`\n\nWrite the final room assignment package after applying the update.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One final room assignment for every session.\n- The final total room cost and remaining budget.\n- A short note confirming the same workshop objective is still covered.\n- A short note naming preserved work from the initial plan.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not relax hard room requirements unless a local file explicitly says to.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
